concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11 The arrangements that apply to universal service areas"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-11 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section sets out the arrangements for the fulfilment of the universal service obligation by universal service providers.  (2) The default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to each universal service area in respect of a service obligation.  (3) If the Minister determines under section 11C, for a universal service area in respect of a service obligation, that the obligation is a contestable service obligation, then:  (a) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the area; and  (b) the standard contestability arrangements set out in Division 6 apply to the area in respect of the contestable service obligation.  (4) If the Minister determines under Division 7 that alternative arrangements apply to a universal service area in respect of a service obligation (whether or not it is a contestable service obligation), then:  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            19  (a) those alternative arrangements apply to the area; and  (b) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the area except to the extent that the determination modifies the way those arrangements apply, or excludes them from applying, to the area." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section sets out the arrangements for the fulfilment of the universal service obligation by universal service providers.  (2) The default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to each universal service area in respect of a service obligation.  (3) If the Minister determines under section 11C, for a universal service area in respect of a service obligation, that the obligation is a contestable service obligation, then:  (a) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the area; and  (b) the standard contestability arrangements set out in Division 6 apply to the area in respect of the contestable service obligation.  (4) If the Minister determines under Division 7 that alternative arrangements apply to a universal service area in respect of a service obligation (whether or not it is a contestable service obligation), then:  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            19  (a) those alternative arrangements apply to the area; and  (b) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the area except to the extent that the determination modifies the way those arrangements apply, or excludes them from applying, to the area."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "792bee5b684697c2fba138c4a85a15e406425f087387ac5bcfbf728c3cb000c7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.22" .
doc:sch-1-sec-11 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "11 The arrangements that apply to universal service areas" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section sets out the arrangements for the fulfilment of the universal service obligation by universal service providers.  (2) The default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to each universal service area in respect of a service obligation.  (3) If the Minister determines under section 11C, for a universal service area in respect of a service obligation, that the obligation is a contestable service obligation, then:  (a) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the area; and  (b) the standard contestability arrangements set out in Division 6 apply to the area in respect of the contestable service obligation.  (4) If the Minister determines under Division 7 that alternative arrangements apply to a universal service area in respect of a service obligation (whether or not it is a contestable service obligation), then:  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            19  (a) those alternative arrangements apply to the area; and  (b) the default arrangements set out in Division 5 apply to the area except to the extent that the determination modifies the way those arrangements apply, or excludes them from applying, to the area." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

