concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20-ss-6a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20(6A) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20-ss-6a ;
    values:originalText "(6A) If a former provider has been given notice of a requirement under subsection (3), the ACA may, in writing, direct the former provider to comply with the requirement or with specified aspects of the requirement. The former provider must comply with the direction.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    skos:definition "(6A) If a former provider has been given notice of a requirement under subsection (3), the ACA may, in writing, direct the former provider to comply with the requirement or with specified aspects of the requirement. The former provider must comply with the direction.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c5fbec861469c66e0d2d455410d9e22e0dc287e38df96c307771fc1c5e191cca" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20 ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Former provider must comply with direction from ACA." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
