concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11C Determination of contestable service obligation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-11c ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may determine in writing, for a universal service area in respect of a service obligation, that the obligation is a contestable service obligation. Note 1: This means that the standard contestability arrangements apply to the area in respect of the contestable service obligation (see subsection 11(3)). Note 2: The Minister can make determinations under this section initially only in relation to pilot areas (see section 11F).  (2) The Minister must give to the ACA a copy of each determination made under this section.  (3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may determine in writing, for a universal service area in respect of a service obligation, that the obligation is a contestable service obligation. Note 1: This means that the standard contestability arrangements apply to the area in respect of the contestable service obligation (see subsection 11(3)). Note 2: The Minister can make determinations under this section initially only in relation to pilot areas (see section 11F).  (2) The Minister must give to the ACA a copy of each determination made under this section.  (3) A determination under this section is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
