concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-11e a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11E Transitional arrangements may be determined"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-11e ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 11C, the Minister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            23 issues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.  (2) A copy of a determination under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the Minister revokes a determination under section 11C, the Minister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            23 issues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.  (2) A copy of a determination under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "40fae3a121efb4864bf304999a30db2010e601c36368856c5c7885a2eb239aaa" ;
    cof:pageNumber "26"^^xsd:integer ;
