    values:originalText "(4) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have regard to:  (a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any) under section 12G; and  (b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for the purposes of this paragraph; and  (c) such other matters as the ACA considers relevant." ;
    cof:pageNumber "35"^^xsd:integer .

