doc:sch-1-sec-12l a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "12L Approval of draft standard marketing plan" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft standard marketing plan that a primary universal service provider gives to the ACA.  (2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:  (a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services that the provider will supply in fulfilment of the service obligation concerned, so far as it relates to the universal service area concerned; and  (b) the draft adequately deals with how the provider will fulfil that service obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and  (c) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which the equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and  (d) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing of the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons in the universal service area concerned.  (3) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have regard to:  (a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any) under section 12G; and  (b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for the purposes of this paragraph; and  (c) any other matters the ACA considers relevant.  (4) A copy of a determination made for the purposes of paragraph (3)(b) must be published in the Gazette." ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

