concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12p a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12P Meaning of expressions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12p ;
    values:originalText "(1) A draft ATS marketing plan for a primary universal service provider for a universal service area in respect of a service obligation is a plan that sets out:  (a) the alternative telecommunications services that the provider will supply in fulfilment of that service obligation so far as it relates to that area; and  (b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing those services.  (2) A draft ATS marketing plan that has been approved by the ACA under section 12T, and that is in force, is an approved ATS marketing plan for the primary universal service provider concerned.  (3) Each draft or approved ATS marketing plan must cover only one universal service area and only one service obligation. However, the ACA may determine in writing that this subsection does not apply to:  (a) draft or approved ATS marketing plans generally; or  (b) a draft or approved ATS marketing plan of a particular primary universal service provider.  (4) A copy of a determination made under subsection (3) must be published in the Gazette." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A draft ATS marketing plan for a primary universal service provider for a universal service area in respect of a service obligation is a plan that sets out:  (a) the alternative telecommunications services that the provider will supply in fulfilment of that service obligation so far as it relates to that area; and  (b) the arrangements for supplying and marketing those services.  (2) A draft ATS marketing plan that has been approved by the ACA under section 12T, and that is in force, is an approved ATS marketing plan for the primary universal service provider concerned.  (3) Each draft or approved ATS marketing plan must cover only one universal service area and only one service obligation. However, the ACA may determine in writing that this subsection does not apply to:  (a) draft or approved ATS marketing plans generally; or  (b) a draft or approved ATS marketing plan of a particular primary universal service provider.  (4) A copy of a determination made under subsection (3) must be published in the Gazette."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bbe44596e5cfb5c1cd8ed98bec827542233d83947667583918d7cfbd3ee0af51" ;
    cof:pageNumber "37"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12p-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12p-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12p-ss-3 ;
