concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12s a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12S Public consultation required on draft ATS marketing plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12s ;
    values:originalText "(1) Before deciding whether to approve a draft ATS marketing plan, the ACA must require the provider concerned:  (a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite members of the public to make submissions to the applicant about the preliminary version within a specified period (which must be at least 30 days); and  (b) to give consideration to any submissions received from members of the public within that period; and  (c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes made to the draft as a result.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            35  (2) Subsection (1) applies only if a draft ATS marketing plan is materially different from an ATS marketing plan previously approved by the ACA." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Before deciding whether to approve a draft ATS marketing plan, the ACA must require the provider concerned:  (a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft and invite members of the public to make submissions to the applicant about the preliminary version within a specified period (which must be at least 30 days); and  (b) to give consideration to any submissions received from members of the public within that period; and  (c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes made to the draft as a result.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            35  (2) Subsection (1) applies only if a draft ATS marketing plan is materially different from an ATS marketing plan previously approved by the ACA."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6c565b8bd3eb8d79c5c8a8614802f7308cb9c44c0f1366863aa10ae8a0ce659b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12s-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12s-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
