concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12w a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12W Variation of approved policy statement, approved standard"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12w ;
    values:originalText "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan  (1) This section applies if:  (a) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service provider (the current statement) is in force; or  (b) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; or  (c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a primary universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; and the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current statement or current plan.  (2) The ACA must:  (a) approve the variation; or  (b) refuse to approve the variation.  (3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if the ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:  (a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and invite members of the public to make submissions to the provider about the preliminary version within a specified period; and  (b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of the public received within that period; and  (c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes made to the draft variation as a result.  (4) The ACA must not approve the variation unless it is satisfied that:  (a) in the case of a draft variation of an approved policy statement—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    skos:definition "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan  (1) This section applies if:  (a) an approved policy statement for a primary universal service provider (the current statement) is in force; or  (b) an approved standard marketing plan for a primary universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; or  (c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a primary universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; and the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current statement or current plan.  (2) The ACA must:  (a) approve the variation; or  (b) refuse to approve the variation.  (3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if the ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:  (a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and invite members of the public to make submissions to the provider about the preliminary version within a specified period; and  (b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of the public received within that period; and  (c) to advise the ACA on those submissions and any changes made to the draft variation as a result.  (4) The ACA must not approve the variation unless it is satisfied that:  (a) in the case of a draft variation of an approved policy statement—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "669de56158c34ccc1a4c6a047420e99252318118d4ee37a4a7de8edcda59f9d7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "41"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12w-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12w-ss-2 ;
