doc:sch-1-sec-38 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "38 Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(No. 2) 2000       No. 142, 2000 policy statement in the same terms as the current statement as varied, the ACA would approve that draft; or  (b) in the case of a draft variation of an approved standard marketing plan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft standard marketing plan in the same terms as the current plan as varied, the ACA would approve that draft; or  (c) in the case of a draft variation of an approved ATS marketing plan—if the provider were to give the ACA a draft ATS marketing plan in the same terms as the current plan as varied, the ACA would approve that draft." ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12x a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "12X Notice of decision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-12x ;
    values:originalText "(1) After deciding whether to approve a variation under section 12W, the ACA must give a written notice setting out the decision to the provider concerned.  (2) If the ACA refuses to approve the variation, the ACA must give a written notice setting out the reasons for the refusal to the provider.  (3) If the ACA approves the variation:  (a) the current statement or plan is varied accordingly; and  (b) a copy of the notice given to the provider must be published in the Gazette, unless the variation is only of a minor technical nature." ;
    skos:definition "(1) After deciding whether to approve a variation under section 12W, the ACA must give a written notice setting out the decision to the provider concerned.  (2) If the ACA refuses to approve the variation, the ACA must give a written notice setting out the reasons for the refusal to the provider.  (3) If the ACA approves the variation:  (a) the current statement or plan is varied accordingly; and  (b) a copy of the notice given to the provider must be published in the Gazette, unless the variation is only of a minor technical nature."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3f1b3ca141ce79802763e69df181d0887a1b172342520b5647f3aa34d7b29c19" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12x-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12x-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-12x-ss-3 ;
