concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13C Date of effect of approval, or variation or revocation of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13c ;
    values:originalText "approval  (1) An approval under section 13B takes effect on the day specified in the approval. That day must be on or after the day on which the approval is given.  (2) If an approval is expressed to cease to have effect at a specified time, it ceases to have effect at that time.  (3) A variation or revocation of an approval takes effect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument of variation or revocation. That day must be on or after the day on which the instrument is made.  (4) If the ACA revokes an approval under section 13B, it may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    skos:definition "approval  (1) An approval under section 13B takes effect on the day specified in the approval. That day must be on or after the day on which the approval is given.  (2) If an approval is expressed to cease to have effect at a specified time, it ceases to have effect at that time.  (3) A variation or revocation of an approval takes effect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument of variation or revocation. That day must be on or after the day on which the instrument is made.  (4) If the ACA revokes an approval under section 13B, it may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9deb65b8788f41ff94a217842017db2f843954fc0eb46110835903908e5a265f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "45"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13c-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.45" .
doc:sch-1-sec-13c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "13C Date of effect of approval, or variation or revocation of" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "approval  (1) An approval under section 13B takes effect on the day specified in the approval. That day must be on or after the day on which the approval is given.  (2) If an approval is expressed to cease to have effect at a specified time, it ceases to have effect at that time.  (3) A variation or revocation of an approval takes effect on the day specified for the purpose in the instrument of variation or revocation. That day must be on or after the day on which the instrument is made.  (4) If the ACA revokes an approval under section 13B, it may determine in writing arrangements to deal with any issues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    cof:pageNumber "45"^^xsd:integer .

