concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13F Meaning of expressions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13f ;
    values:originalText "(1) A draft policy statement for an applicant for approval as a competing universal service provider is a general statement of the policy the applicant will apply in supplying equipment, goods or services as a competing universal service provider.  (2) A draft policy statement that has been approved by the ACA under section 13J, and that is in force, is an approved policy statement for the applicant or competing universal service provider concerned.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A draft policy statement for an applicant for approval as a competing universal service provider is a general statement of the policy the applicant will apply in supplying equipment, goods or services as a competing universal service provider.  (2) A draft policy statement that has been approved by the ACA under section 13J, and that is in force, is an approved policy statement for the applicant or competing universal service provider concerned.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f24e83487c5a307a1178bcad5d087d69cb384699f2089db975d98fa96f95942d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "47"^^xsd:integer ;
