concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13G Minister may determine requirements for drafts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13g ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may determine in writing requirements for draft policy statements and draft standard marketing plans of competing universal service providers.  (2) These are some examples of requirements for draft standard marketing plans:  (a) timeframes for the supply of specified equipment, goods or services;  (b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the universal service obligation;  (c) processes for advising persons about the availability, offer and supply of equipment, goods or services in the fulfilment of the universal service obligation, and the terms and conditions on which the equipment, goods or services are offered or supplied;  (d) the form of a draft standard marketing plan.  (3) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            45" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may determine in writing requirements for draft policy statements and draft standard marketing plans of competing universal service providers.  (2) These are some examples of requirements for draft standard marketing plans:  (a) timeframes for the supply of specified equipment, goods or services;  (b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the universal service obligation;  (c) processes for advising persons about the availability, offer and supply of equipment, goods or services in the fulfilment of the universal service obligation, and the terms and conditions on which the equipment, goods or services are offered or supplied;  (d) the form of a draft standard marketing plan.  (3) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            45"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b7fe399707b4643cdfab173b6eeefa028e5c935c8e80bd4410ea15602a1c9e00" ;
    cof:pageNumber "48"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13g-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13g-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13g-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.48" .
doc:sch-1-sec-13g a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "13G Minister may determine requirements for drafts" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may determine in writing requirements for draft policy statements and draft standard marketing plans of competing universal service providers.  (2) These are some examples of requirements for draft standard marketing plans:  (a) timeframes for the supply of specified equipment, goods or services;  (b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the universal service obligation;  (c) processes for advising persons about the availability, offer and supply of equipment, goods or services in the fulfilment of the universal service obligation, and the terms and conditions on which the equipment, goods or services are offered or supplied;  (d) the form of a draft standard marketing plan.  (3) A determination under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            45" ;
    cof:pageNumber "48"^^xsd:integer .

