concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13J Approval of draft policy statement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13j ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft policy statement that an applicant for approval as a competing universal service provider gives to the ACA.  (2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that the draft adequately deals with the supply of appropriate equipment, goods or services to:  (a) people with a disability; and  (b) people with special needs.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACA must approve, or refuse to approve, a draft policy statement that an applicant for approval as a competing universal service provider gives to the ACA.  (2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that the draft adequately deals with the supply of appropriate equipment, goods or services to:  (a) people with a disability; and  (b) people with special needs.  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2cec1d99f7a2a21bb99fb9b34cb3fc1658a56c816d14312cf65d57507e88a685" ;
    cof:pageNumber "49"^^xsd:integer ;
