    skos:definition "(2) The ACA must not approve the draft unless it is satisfied that:  (a) the draft specifies appropriate equipment, goods or services that the applicant will supply in fulfilment of the contestable service obligation concerned, so far as it relates to the universal service area concerned; and  (b) the draft adequately deals with how the applicant will fulfil that contestable service obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and  (c) the draft sets out appropriate terms and conditions on which the equipment, goods or services are to be supplied; and  (d) the draft sets out appropriate arrangements for the marketing of the supply of the equipment, goods or services to persons in that area; and  (e) the draft sets out appropriate procedures that the applicant will comply with if the applicant ceases:  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            47  (i) to supply any of the equipment, goods or services; or  (ii) to fulfil that contestable service obligation, so far as it relates to that area;  including the giving of at least 45 days’ notice to the ACA, or such other notice as the ACA determines in writing is adequate."@en ;
