    skos:definition "(3) In deciding whether to approve the draft, the ACA must also have regard to:  (a) whether the draft complies with the requirements (if any) under section 13G; and  (b) any other matters determined in writing by the Minister for the purposes of this paragraph; and  (c) any other matters the ACA considers relevant."@en ;
