doc:sch-1-sec-13m a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "13M Meaning of expressions" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A draft ATS marketing plan for an applicant for approval as a competing universal service provider for a universal service area in respect of a contestable service obligation is a plan that sets out:  (a) the alternative telecommunications services that the applicant will supply in fulfilment of that contestable service obligation, so far as it relates to that area; and  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
