doc:sch-1-sec-48-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "48(2) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) A draft ATS marketing plan that has been approved by the ACA under section 13Q, and that is in force, is an approved ATS marketing plan for the applicant or competing universal service provider concerned." ;
    cof:pageNumber "52"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-48-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "48(3) Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-48-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) Each draft or approved ATS marketing plan must cover only one universal service area and only one contestable service obligation. However, the ACA may determine in writing that this subsection does not apply to:  (a) draft or approved ATS marketing plans generally; or  (b) a draft or approved ATS marketing plan of a particular applicant or competing universal service provider." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Each draft or approved ATS marketing plan must cover only one universal service area and only one contestable service obligation. However, the ACA may determine in writing that this subsection does not apply to:  (a) draft or approved ATS marketing plans generally; or  (b) a draft or approved ATS marketing plan of a particular applicant or competing universal service provider."@en ;
