concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13r a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13R Notice of decision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13r ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACA must give the applicant written notice of the ACA’s decision on whether to approve the draft ATS marketing plan.  (2) If the ACA refuses to approve the draft, the ACA must give the applicant written notice of the reasons for that refusal.  (3) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette, if the decision is to approve the draft.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            51 Subdivision E—Replacement, variation and revocation of policy statements, standard marketing plans and ATS marketing plans" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACA must give the applicant written notice of the ACA’s decision on whether to approve the draft ATS marketing plan.  (2) If the ACA refuses to approve the draft, the ACA must give the applicant written notice of the reasons for that refusal.  (3) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette, if the decision is to approve the draft.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            51 Subdivision E—Replacement, variation and revocation of policy statements, standard marketing plans and ATS marketing plans"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5d4fb118fb4203cfe09787fc769a087db5a3e3278c6314bde794e61880f5d054" ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
