concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13t a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13T Variation of approved policy statement, approved standard"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13t ;
    values:originalText "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan  (1) This section applies if:  (a) an approved policy statement for a competing universal service provider (the current statement) is in force; or  (b) an approved standard marketing plan for a competing universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; or  (c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a competing universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; and the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current statement or current plan.  (2) The ACA must:  (a) approve the variation; or  (b) refuse to approve the variation.  (3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if the ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    skos:definition "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan  (1) This section applies if:  (a) an approved policy statement for a competing universal service provider (the current statement) is in force; or  (b) an approved standard marketing plan for a competing universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; or  (c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a competing universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; and the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current statement or current plan.  (2) The ACA must:  (a) approve the variation; or  (b) refuse to approve the variation.  (3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if the ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "669de56158c34ccc1a4c6a047420e99252318118d4ee37a4a7de8edcda59f9d7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13t-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13t-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13t-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.55" .
doc:sch-1-sec-13t a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "13T Variation of approved policy statement, approved standard" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "marketing plan or approved ATS marketing plan  (1) This section applies if:  (a) an approved policy statement for a competing universal service provider (the current statement) is in force; or  (b) an approved standard marketing plan for a competing universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; or  (c) an approved ATS marketing plan for a competing universal service provider (the current plan) is in force; and the provider gives the ACA a draft variation of the current statement or current plan.  (2) The ACA must:  (a) approve the variation; or  (b) refuse to approve the variation.  (3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the ACA may, if the ACA considers it appropriate, require the provider:  Schedule 1  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999" ;
    cof:pageNumber "55"^^xsd:integer .

