concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13v a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "13V Minister may revoke approved ATS marketing plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-13v ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by giving written notice to a competing universal service provider, revoke the provider’s approved ATS  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            53 marketing plan if the Minister considers that it is in the public interest to do so. A copy of the notice must be given to the ACA.  (2) An approved ATS marketing plan that is revoked by the Minister ceases to be in force when the revocation takes effect.  (3) The revocation takes effect on the day specified in the notice which must be on or after the day on which the notice is given to the provider.  (4) The Minister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with issues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation. A copy of the determination must be:  (a) given to the provider; and  (b) published in the Gazette.  (5) The provider must comply with the arrangements (if any) in a determination under subsection (4)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by giving written notice to a competing universal service provider, revoke the provider’s approved ATS  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            53 marketing plan if the Minister considers that it is in the public interest to do so. A copy of the notice must be given to the ACA.  (2) An approved ATS marketing plan that is revoked by the Minister ceases to be in force when the revocation takes effect.  (3) The revocation takes effect on the day specified in the notice which must be on or after the day on which the notice is given to the provider.  (4) The Minister may determine in writing arrangements to deal with issues of a transitional nature that may arise as a result of the revocation. A copy of the determination must be:  (a) given to the provider; and  (b) published in the Gazette.  (5) The provider must comply with the arrangements (if any) in a determination under subsection (4)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8a3d930d3c02f76afb9ed514726ea817282ccf5eb8da2b95913d34e81006d2c3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "56"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13v-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13v-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-13v-ss-3 ;
