doc:sch-1-sec-15b-ss-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15B(5) Former digital data service provider may be required to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) The current provider may, by written notice given to the former provider, require the former provider to give to the current provider specified information of the kind referred to in subsection (6). A notice of this kind cannot be given more than 6 months after:  (a) if subsection (1) applies—the later of the following days:  (i) the day on which the current provider became a digital data service provider for the relevant area; or  (ii) the day on which the determination under subsection 15(1) or (2) was made in respect of the current provider; or  (b) if subsection (2) applies—the day on which the former provider ceases to be a digital data service provider for the relevant area." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15b-ss-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15B(6) Former digital data service provider may be required to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-15b-ss-6 ;
    values:originalText "(6) The information that may be required to be given must be information that will assist the current provider in doing something that the current provider is or will be required or permitted to do by or under a provision of this Part. The notice must identify the doing of that thing as the purpose for which the information is required. Note 1: If, for example, information about service location and customer contact details will assist the current provider in fulfilling its obligation under subsection 15A(4) or (5), the former provider may be required to provide that kind of information. Note 2: See also subsection (8), which allows the Minister to determine that a specified kind of information is information referred to in this subsection." ;
    skos:definition "(6) The information that may be required to be given must be information that will assist the current provider in doing something that the current provider is or will be required or permitted to do by or under a provision of this Part. The notice must identify the doing of that thing as the purpose for which the information is required. Note 1: If, for example, information about service location and customer contact details will assist the current provider in fulfilling its obligation under subsection 15A(4) or (5), the former provider may be required to provide that kind of information. Note 2: See also subsection (8), which allows the Minister to determine that a specified kind of information is information referred to in this subsection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "690b0b96dd290308d227d0bb9cb04a3c6045ed393daf62a02a029d6ec9212311" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15b ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Former digital data service provider must provide information to assist in fulfilling obligations." ;
    dc:description "True" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
