    values:originalText "(1) In deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for a general digital data service area or a special digital data service area, the Minister must have regard to whether:  (a) the draft plan provides for the general digital data service obligation, or special digital data service obligation, (so far as it relates to that area) to be fulfilled:  (i) as efficiently and economically as practicable; and  (ii) at performance standards that reasonably meet the social, industrial and commercial needs of the Australian community; and  (iii) progressively throughout that area within such period as the Minister considers reasonable; and  (aa) the draft plan addresses the needs of people with a disability; and  (b) the draft plan complies with any requirements in force under section 15J." ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15h-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
