concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15j a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15J Minister may formulate requirements for draft plans"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-15j ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by writing, formulate requirements for draft digital data service plans.  (2) The following are examples of requirements:  (a) timetables for the supply of services;  (b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the digital data service obligation;  (c) the form of a draft digital data service plan.  (3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by writing, formulate requirements for draft digital data service plans.  (2) The following are examples of requirements:  (a) timetables for the supply of services;  (b) performance standards relating to the fulfilment of the digital data service obligation;  (c) the form of a draft digital data service plan.  (3) An instrument under subsection (1) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "92cc4aa331378b7f5463696381227ee07fb46d11e87702b16374af83d866a216" ;
