concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15K Notification of decision"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-15k ;
    values:originalText "(1) After deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the decision to:  (a) the digital data service provider concerned; and  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            61  (b) the ACA.  (2) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette.  (3) If the Minister refuses to approve a draft digital data service plan for an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the reasons for the refusal to the digital data service provider concerned." ;
    skos:definition "(1) After deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the decision to:  (a) the digital data service provider concerned; and  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            61  (b) the ACA.  (2) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette.  (3) If the Minister refuses to approve a draft digital data service plan for an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the reasons for the refusal to the digital data service provider concerned."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "96c94b71a7b4d6ce21a54a3c5c28c16373772edc8b6b28bd4866c3ad288f2901" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15k-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.64" .
doc:sch-1-sec-15k a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15K Notification of decision" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) After deciding whether to approve a draft digital data service plan for an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the decision to:  (a) the digital data service provider concerned; and  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            61  (b) the ACA.  (2) A copy of a notice under subsection (1) must be published in the Gazette.  (3) If the Minister refuses to approve a draft digital data service plan for an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the reasons for the refusal to the digital data service provider concerned." ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

