doc:sch-1-sec-15k-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "15K(3) Notification of decision" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Minister refuses to approve a draft digital data service plan for an area, the Minister must give a written notice setting out the reasons for the refusal to the digital data service provider concerned." ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15L Variation of approved digital data service plan"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-15l ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) an approved digital data service plan for an area (the current plan) is in force; and  (b) the digital data service provider concerned gives the Minister a draft variation of the plan.  (2) The Minister must:  (a) approve the variation; or  (b) refuse to approve the variation.  (3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the Minister may, if he or she considers it appropriate, require the provider:  (a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and invite members of the public to make submissions to the provider about the preliminary version within a specified period; and  (b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of the public received within that period; and  (c) to advise the Minister on those submissions and any changes made to the draft variation as a result.  (4) The Minister must not approve the variation unless the Minister is satisfied that, if the provider were to give the Minister a draft digital data service plan in the same terms as the current plan as proposed to be varied, the Minister would approve that draft." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) an approved digital data service plan for an area (the current plan) is in force; and  (b) the digital data service provider concerned gives the Minister a draft variation of the plan.  (2) The Minister must:  (a) approve the variation; or  (b) refuse to approve the variation.  (3) Before deciding whether to approve the variation, the Minister may, if he or she considers it appropriate, require the provider:  (a) to publish a preliminary version of the draft variation and invite members of the public to make submissions to the provider about the preliminary version within a specified period; and  (b) to give consideration to any submissions from members of the public received within that period; and  (c) to advise the Minister on those submissions and any changes made to the draft variation as a result.  (4) The Minister must not approve the variation unless the Minister is satisfied that, if the provider were to give the Minister a draft digital data service plan in the same terms as the current plan as proposed to be varied, the Minister would approve that draft."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "be4fa3c6a6cafd06680097c193cf0a99764422d6e3e687f272fb9b48cad34bbf" ;
    cof:pageNumber "65"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-15l-ss-4 ;
