concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 Determination of universal service subsidy"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-16-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Before the end of a claim period, the Minister must determine in writing one or more universal service subsidies for the period. A  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            63 copy of a determination under this subsection must be published in the Gazette.  (2) The Minister must ensure that there is a subsidy for each universal service area in respect of each service obligation. A subsidy may cover one or more universal service areas in respect of one or more service obligations.  (3) A determination under this section must specify:  (a) the amount, or a method for working out the amount, of the subsidy; and  (b) the circumstances in which a universal service provider for the claim period is eligible to be paid the subsidy.  (4) The circumstances that may be specified include, but are not limited to:  (a) whether the subsidy is payable to a primary universal service provider or a competing universal service provider; and  (b) the types or amount of equipment, goods or services that are supplied to persons in a universal service area.  (5) The determination must specify that a subsidy is only payable to a universal service provider who complies with the provider’s obligations under section 12C or 13D (whichever is applicable).  (6) A determination may specify an amount of subsidy as zero." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Before the end of a claim period, the Minister must determine in writing one or more universal service subsidies for the period. A  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            63 copy of a determination under this subsection must be published in the Gazette.  (2) The Minister must ensure that there is a subsidy for each universal service area in respect of each service obligation. A subsidy may cover one or more universal service areas in respect of one or more service obligations.  (3) A determination under this section must specify:  (a) the amount, or a method for working out the amount, of the subsidy; and  (b) the circumstances in which a universal service provider for the claim period is eligible to be paid the subsidy.  (4) The circumstances that may be specified include, but are not limited to:  (a) whether the subsidy is payable to a primary universal service provider or a competing universal service provider; and  (b) the types or amount of equipment, goods or services that are supplied to persons in a universal service area.  (5) The determination must specify that a subsidy is only payable to a universal service provider who complies with the provider’s obligations under section 12C or 13D (whichever is applicable).  (6) A determination may specify an amount of subsidy as zero."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ce3c15f81ab55c84f9fa4d162f35ead256a1377b4d4da253b526b81fa34fdd62" ;
    cof:pageNumber "66"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-16-2-ss-3 ;
