    values:originalText "(1) A person’s digital data cost for a claim period depends on which of the following paragraphs is applicable for that claim period:  (a) if:  (i) the person is a digital data service provider for that claim period; and  (ii) a determination is in force under subsection (4) in relation to that claim period;  the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is worked out in accordance with the determination;  (b) if:  (i) the person is a digital data service provider for that claim period; and  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            65  (ii) no determination is in force under subsection (4) in relation to that claim period;  then:  (iii) if the amount worked out using the formula in subsection (2) is greater than zero—the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is equal to that amount; or  (iv) if the amount worked out using the formula in subsection (2) is not greater than zero—the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is zero. Note: The digital data cost is needed for the purposes of making a claim for levy credit for a claim period (see section 20J)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person’s digital data cost for a claim period depends on which of the following paragraphs is applicable for that claim period:  (a) if:  (i) the person is a digital data service provider for that claim period; and  (ii) a determination is in force under subsection (4) in relation to that claim period;  the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is worked out in accordance with the determination;  (b) if:  (i) the person is a digital data service provider for that claim period; and  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            65  (ii) no determination is in force under subsection (4) in relation to that claim period;  then:  (iii) if the amount worked out using the formula in subsection (2) is greater than zero—the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is equal to that amount; or  (iv) if the amount worked out using the formula in subsection (2) is not greater than zero—the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is zero. Note: The digital data cost is needed for the purposes of making a claim for levy credit for a claim period (see section 20J)."@en ;
