doc:sch-1-sec-17-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "17(1) Digital data cost of a digital data service provider for a claim" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person’s digital data cost for a claim period depends on which of the following paragraphs is applicable for that claim period:  (a) if:  (i) the person is a digital data service provider for that claim period; and  (ii) a determination is in force under subsection (4) in relation to that claim period;  the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is worked out in accordance with the determination;  (b) if:  (i) the person is a digital data service provider for that claim period; and  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            65  (ii) no determination is in force under subsection (4) in relation to that claim period;  then:  (iii) if the amount worked out using the formula in subsection (2) is greater than zero—the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is equal to that amount; or  (iv) if the amount worked out using the formula in subsection (2) is not greater than zero—the person’s digital data cost for the claim period is zero. Note: The digital data cost is needed for the purposes of making a claim for levy credit for a claim period (see section 20J)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "17(2) Digital data cost of a digital data service provider for a claim"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-17-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The formula referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is as follows: Customer equipment costs Customer charges Supplementary amount – +  where: customer charges means the total amount payable by persons in the area referred to in subsection (3) by way of charges for the supply by the person during the claim period of customer equipment covered by paragraph (3)(a). customer equipment costs means the person’s customer equipment costs for the claim period. supplementary amount means the amount (if any) specified in, or ascertained in accordance with, regulations made for the purposes of this definition." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The formula referred to in paragraph (1)(b) is as follows: Customer equipment costs Customer charges Supplementary amount – +  where: customer charges means the total amount payable by persons in the area referred to in subsection (3) by way of charges for the supply by the person during the claim period of customer equipment covered by paragraph (3)(a). customer equipment costs means the person’s customer equipment costs for the claim period. supplementary amount means the amount (if any) specified in, or ascertained in accordance with, regulations made for the purposes of this definition."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a2b593178510ec76b395f15c09539e1bddfd1cca1e0fe3ea0b5f9009ee4bcdd0" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-17 ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Customer charges and equipment costs calculation formula" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
