concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-18-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "18 Universal service charges"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-18-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if a person is the universal service provider for a universal service area.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            67  (2) For the purposes of this Division, a universal service charge is a charge imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the person for:  (a) the supply of standard telephone services to persons in the area; or  (b) calls made from payphones in the area; or  (c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to persons in the area." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if a person is the universal service provider for a universal service area.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            67  (2) For the purposes of this Division, a universal service charge is a charge imposed, or proposed to be imposed, by the person for:  (a) the supply of standard telephone services to persons in the area; or  (b) calls made from payphones in the area; or  (c) the supply of prescribed carriage services to persons in the area."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f71554dee21c9043822f822ef7e52576deff0e24cc48d588431a80e6d00da097" ;
