    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A determination under section 18B relating to a universal service charge may:  (a) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the Minister’s consent; or  (b) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without the ACCC’s consent; or  (c) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without prior notice being given to the Minister; or  (d) prohibit the charge from being imposed or altered without prior notice being given to the ACCC; or  (e) empower the Minister to direct the ACCC to give the Minister such reports and advice as the Minister requires for the purposes of assisting the Minister in deciding whether to give a consent in accordance with the determination.  (2) Subsection (1) does not, by implication, limit section 18B." ;
    cof:pageNumber "72"^^xsd:integer .

