concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20K Audit report of claim"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20k ;
    values:originalText "(1) A claim must be accompanied by a report of an approved auditor that:  (a) is in a form approved in writing by the ACA; and  (b) states that the auditor has audited the claim; and  (c) contains a determination, in the terms specified in the form, of the auditor’s opinion; and  (d) states that the auditor has been given sufficient information and assistance in order to audit the claim; and  (e) includes all other statements and information required by the form to be included.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            77  (2) However, the Minister may, by making a written determination, modify the requirements in subsection (1), including by omitting, adding or substituting requirements.  (3) This section does not apply to a person if the ACA gives written notice to the person to that effect.  (4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published in the Gazette." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A claim must be accompanied by a report of an approved auditor that:  (a) is in a form approved in writing by the ACA; and  (b) states that the auditor has audited the claim; and  (c) contains a determination, in the terms specified in the form, of the auditor’s opinion; and  (d) states that the auditor has been given sufficient information and assistance in order to audit the claim; and  (e) includes all other statements and information required by the form to be included.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            77  (2) However, the Minister may, by making a written determination, modify the requirements in subsection (1), including by omitting, adding or substituting requirements.  (3) This section does not apply to a person if the ACA gives written notice to the person to that effect.  (4) A copy of a determination under subsection (2) must be published in the Gazette."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d5d2e543138e510f703f7c396dd2093d7abe29bcd20bc352e3f822d5a59c7373" ;
    cof:pageNumber "80"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20k-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.80" .
