doc:sch-1-sec-20u-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "20U(2) ACA to make written assessment" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) For each participating person for the last eligible revenue period that ended before the start of the claim period, the assessment must set out:  (a) the person’s levy debit under section 20R for the claim period; and  (b) the person’s levy debit balance (if any) under section 20S for the claim period; and  (c) if the person has a levy debit balance—the levy payable by the person on that balance. Note: Section 20Z sets out when the levy is payable." ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20u-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20U(3) ACA to make written assessment"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20u-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) For each universal service provider for the claim period, the assessment must set out:  (a) the universal service subsidy to which the ACA assesses the provider is entitled for the claim period; and  (b) the provider’s levy credit balance (if any) under section 20T for the claim period; and  (c) if the provider has a levy credit balance—the amount payable to the provider under section 21C for the claim period." ;
    skos:definition "(3) For each universal service provider for the claim period, the assessment must set out:  (a) the universal service subsidy to which the ACA assesses the provider is entitled for the claim period; and  (b) the provider’s levy credit balance (if any) under section 20T for the claim period; and  (c) if the provider has a levy credit balance—the amount payable to the provider under section 21C for the claim period."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fb44753a5f3a312da376846ce336eb684e9a9de16001c64ce823f2c739a5d202" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-20u ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Universal service provider must set out assessment details" ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
