concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21D Distribution of remaining balance of the Universal Service"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-21d ;
    values:originalText "Account  (1) The ACA may distribute to persons who are or were participating persons any balance of the Universal Service Account that remains after all amounts payable out of it for a claim period have been paid.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            87  (2) The Minister may determine in writing rules for making those distributions. The ACA must comply with those rules.  (3) A determination under subsection (2) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    skos:definition "Account  (1) The ACA may distribute to persons who are or were participating persons any balance of the Universal Service Account that remains after all amounts payable out of it for a claim period have been paid.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            87  (2) The Minister may determine in writing rules for making those distributions. The ACA must comply with those rules.  (3) A determination under subsection (2) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7e1b0d5641f2640ce9a953ec231eea2c27a2a7633f7d3c273e5735e2b30c10b7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "90"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-1-sec-21d-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf, p.90" .
doc:sch-1-sec-21d a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "21D Distribution of remaining balance of the Universal Service" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Account  (1) The ACA may distribute to persons who are or were participating persons any balance of the Universal Service Account that remains after all amounts payable out of it for a claim period have been paid.  New Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999  Schedule 1  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            87  (2) The Minister may determine in writing rules for making those distributions. The ACA must comply with those rules.  (3) A determination under subsection (2) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901." ;
    cof:pageNumber "90"^^xsd:integer .

