    skos:definition "(1) The ACA may comply with a request by a person under section 22 or 22A by:  (a) communicating information to the person in writing or in some other form; or  (b) making documents available for inspection by the person or by an employee, agent or professional adviser of the person; or  (c) giving to the person copies of, extracts from, or summaries of, documents."@en ;
