doc:sch-2-sec-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "1 Application of repealed Part 2" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Despite the repeal and substitution of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999 by Schedule 1 to this Act, that Part continues to apply, after that Schedule commences in relation to the financial year that ended on 30 June 2000, as if that repeal and substitution had not happened." ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 Things done under repealed Part 2"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) something was done (other than something covered by item 3), before this Act received the Royal Assent, under or for the purposes of a provision of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999; and  (b) immediately after the repeal and substitution of that Part by Schedule 1 to this Act, there is a provision in that Part that requires or allows the same, or an equivalent, thing to be done; then, after the commencement of Schedule 1, the thing is taken to have been done under or for the purposes of the latter provision. (2) If the thing would have been done by another person or body, had it been done after the commencement of Schedule 1, then it is taken to have been done by that other person or body for the purposes of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) something was done (other than something covered by item 3), before this Act received the Royal Assent, under or for the purposes of a provision of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999; and  (b) immediately after the repeal and substitution of that Part by Schedule 1 to this Act, there is a provision in that Part that requires or allows the same, or an equivalent, thing to be done; then, after the commencement of Schedule 1, the thing is taken to have been done under or for the purposes of the latter provision. (2) If the thing would have been done by another person or body, had it been done after the commencement of Schedule 1, then it is taken to have been done by that other person or body for the purposes of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a93f28e0296a503e5bf1e2cd8952c07dadbf0cac438f3f098588f8f888586166" ;
    cof:pageNumber "98"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "If something was done before the Act received Royal Assent, under or for the purposes of a provision of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999, then it is taken to have been done under or for the purposes of the latter provision." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
