concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 References to certain terms in eligible instruments"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-4 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations, a declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other instrument that:  (a) was in force immediately before this Act received the Royal Assent; and  (b) contains a reference to a term the definition of which is repealed by this Act. (2) For the purposes of the amendments made by Schedule 1 to this Act, the Minister or the ACA may determine in writing that a specified eligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences, as if a reference in the instrument to a specified term were a reference to another specified term. Note: An instrument may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations, a declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other instrument that:  (a) was in force immediately before this Act received the Royal Assent; and  (b) contains a reference to a term the definition of which is repealed by this Act. (2) For the purposes of the amendments made by Schedule 1 to this Act, the Minister or the ACA may determine in writing that a specified eligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences, as if a reference in the instrument to a specified term were a reference to another specified term. Note: An instrument may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1b1e4a41f1222ead826308feef3880067c6fa685b988ba76633faef0a9dbb6f6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definition of eligible instrument" ;
