doc:sch-2-sec-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4 References to certain terms in eligible instruments" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this item, an eligible instrument means regulations, a declaration, a determination, a direction, a notice or any other instrument that:  (a) was in force immediately before this Act received the Royal Assent; and  (b) contains a reference to a term the definition of which is repealed by this Act. (2) For the purposes of the amendments made by Schedule 1 to this Act, the Minister or the ACA may determine in writing that a specified eligible instrument has effect, after that Schedule commences, as if a reference in the instrument to a specified term were a reference to another specified term. Note: An instrument may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way." ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-2-sec-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 Treatment of draft universal service plans"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-5 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This item applies to a draft universal service plan given to the Minister under Division 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999, that the Minister has neither approved nor refused to approve, before this Act received the Royal Assent.  Application and transitional provisions  Schedule 2  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            97 (2) To the extent that the draft contains statements of the policy that the universal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment, goods or services, the draft is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences, taken to be a draft policy statement for the purposes of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999. (3) The remainder of the draft is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be a draft standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This item applies to a draft universal service plan given to the Minister under Division 4 of Part 2 of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999, that the Minister has neither approved nor refused to approve, before this Act received the Royal Assent.  Application and transitional provisions  Schedule 2  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            97 (2) To the extent that the draft contains statements of the policy that the universal service provider concerned will apply in supplying equipment, goods or services, the draft is, after Schedule 1 to this Act commences, taken to be a draft policy statement for the purposes of the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999. (3) The remainder of the draft is, after Schedule 1 commences, taken to be a draft standard marketing plan for the purposes of that Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9a32ac212500d178c2b47f22a4533a8257fbd7f678f466a96427b5ed4796835e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The draft universal service plan must be taken to be a policy statement or standard marketing plan after Schedule 1 commences." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
