doc:sch-4-sec-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5 Distributions before all levies have been paid" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Despite paragraph 215(b) of the former law, an amount is payable from the Universal Service Account for the 1998-1999 financial year even if all of the participating carriers in respect of which the levy was assessed have not yet paid the levy." ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-4-sec-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 Working out how much levy is payable"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-6 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal Service Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service Account, after paying any refunds that are due under section 208 of the former law, the ACA must:  (a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion of the total amounts payable; and  (b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service Account are made in accordance with those proportions (rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers appropriate). (2) However, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for making payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method provided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that determination.  Schedule 4  Levy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal Service Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service Account, after paying any refunds that are due under section 208 of the former law, the ACA must:  (a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion of the total amounts payable; and  (b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service Account are made in accordance with those proportions (rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers appropriate). (2) However, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for making payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method provided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that determination.  Schedule 4  Levy distribution for the 1998-1999 financial year"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cd0d707efa3900315ed1ba0b6b8be05b99ab59aff83b1c43989dfee65c565b9e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "113"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Ensure payments are made in accordance with proportions" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act.pdf> ;
