doc:sch-5-sec-5 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5 Distributions before all levies have been paid" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Despite paragraph 86(b) of the former law, an amount is payable from the Universal Service Account for the 1999-2000 financial year even if all of the participating carriers in respect of which the levy was assessed have not yet paid the levy." ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-consumer-protection-and-service-standards-amendment-act-sch-5-sec-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 Working out how much levy is payable"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-6 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal Service Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service Account, after paying any refunds that are due under section 79 of the former law, the ACA must:  (a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion of the total amounts payable; and  (b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service Account are made in accordance with those proportions (rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers appropriate). (2) However, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for making payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method provided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that determination.  Levy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year  Schedule 5  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            113 (3) A determination under subitem (2) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (4) A carrier’s levy credit balance for the 1999-2000 financial year is reduced by the amount (worked out under this item) that is paid to the carrier. (5) This item continues to apply until each carrier’s levy credit balance for the year is reduced to nil.  [Minister’s second reading speech made in— House of Representatives on 29 June 2000 Senate on 11 October 2000]  (133/00)" ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the total of the amounts payable to carriers out of the Universal Service Account is more than the balance of the Universal Service Account, after paying any refunds that are due under section 79 of the former law, the ACA must:  (a) work out the amount payable to each carrier as a proportion of the total amounts payable; and  (b) ensure that any payments out of the Universal Service Account are made in accordance with those proportions (rounding amounts to whole dollars as the ACA considers appropriate). (2) However, if the Minister determines in writing a different method for making payments out of the Universal Service Account than the method provided in subitem (1), the ACA must act in accordance with that determination.  Levy distribution for the 1999-2000 financial year  Schedule 5  Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Amendment Act (No. 2) 2000 No. 142, 2000            113 (3) A determination under subitem (2) is a disallowable instrument for the purposes of section 46A of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. (4) A carrier’s levy credit balance for the 1999-2000 financial year is reduced by the amount (worked out under this item) that is paid to the carrier. (5) This item continues to apply until each carrier’s levy credit balance for the year is reduced to nil.  [Minister’s second reading speech made in— House of Representatives on 29 June 2000 Senate on 11 October 2000]  (133/00)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "49af11da733a102c605edc88e5619ad96c0996a1227927937bd7d4cff3c85c47" ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Ensure payments are made in accordance with proportions determined by the Minister." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
